96
00:07:27.567 --> 00:07:30.579
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

97
00:07:31.417 --> 00:07:33.648
What defines mastery in a profession?

98
00:07:50.450 --> 00:07:52.020
Now listen to Visal.

99
00:07:52.320 --> 00:08:30.820
Mastery is defined not merely by technical excellence but by the depth of judgement that experience produces. Having solved hundreds of difficult cases, a master recognises patterns that novices miss and knows when the rules should be broken. Equally important is the capacity to teach: a true master raises the standards of the whole profession through mentorship. For example, a great surgeon trains the next generation, not just patients. In my view, mastery becomes complete only when it is shared.

100
00:08:31.120 --> 00:08:32.806
Excellent answer, Visal!

101
00:08:33.717 --> 00:08:38.006
Great work! Now you can use ten new words and participial phrases.

102
00:08:38.306 --> 00:08:43.536
Today's value is mastery. Practise with patience until your skill becomes excellence.

103
